cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use MicroRhodoDB, please cite it using the metadata in this file.
  A companion data-descriptor manuscript is in preparation for submission to
  Database (Oxford) or Scientific Data; this file will be updated with the
  paper citation once it is published.
title: >-
  MicroRhodoDB: a versioned, evidence-aware knowledgebase of Type-I microbial
  rhodopsins
type: dataset
version: 1.6.0
date-released: "2026-10-09"
authors:
  - given-names: CongJian
    family-names: Li
repository-code: "https://github.com/CongjianL/MicroRhodoDB"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - microbial rhodopsins
  - Type-I rhodopsin
  - bacteriorhodopsin
  - phylogenomics
  - protein family database
  - UniProt
  - retinal-binding protein
  - xenorhodopsin
abstract: >-
  MicroRhodoDB curates Type-I microbial rhodopsin proteins from UniProtKB with
  explicit, evidence-graded membership decisions (member/candidate status
  vocabulary), QC features, redundancy handling, a phylogenetically placed
  reference tree (MR_RT_003, ~472 tips) with 19 named subfamilies, a
  five-level function evidence ladder (E1-E5) backed by literature-verified
  assertions, a frozen post-cutoff external validation set, and an isolated
  environmental (MGnify) pilot layer kept separate from the core, evidence-
  graded corpus. Version 1.6.0 adds function-call conflict flags (conflicting
  E3/E4 calls downgraded), an expanded E1 set with labelled publication links,
  engineered-construct flags, a curated membership override for 4
  experimentally characterised E1 proteins, a blind audit of E2-E4 calls, a
  family-HMM flag and Foldseek watchlist for novel families, a full data
  dictionary and a static browser with in-browser sequence search. Releases are
  immutable, versioned SQLite databases; the current release is rebuilt from the
  previous one by a pinned Snakemake workflow.
